# Backends that do NOT yet honour the display backing scale.
#
# Each one renders a 1x image that the compositor upscales, which is the blur
# users see on a HiDPI screen. Deleting a line is the proof the fix landed;
# the gate fails while a line is here but the backend is wired.
#
# mac is deliberately absent: it renders at `backing_scale` (2x on Retina).
#
# linux: the backend has no way to LEARN the density — there is no `wl_output`
# binding anywhere in src/linux/window.zig, so no surface.enter event is
# delivered and `wl_output.scale` is never read. The fix is bounded:
#   1. bind wl_output from the registry (wl_registry_bind, interface wl_output,
#      version 2) and keep the outputs alive;
#   2. add a wl_output_listener with `scale` (and `geometry`) handlers, taking
#      the MAX scale of the outputs the surface has entered;
#   3. on enter/scale, call `render_software.setRenderScale(scale)`;
#   4. size the EGL window with `scale.pixelSize(logical_w, logical_h, scale)`
#      instead of the logical size (wl_egl_window_create / _resize), and make
#      linux/renderer.zig's glViewport use that pixel size;
#   5. delete the `linux` line below.
# Step 5 is the acceptance criterion: the gate will not pass while a backend is
# wired but still listed.
linux
